<title>UK: Lloyd's of London 6th auction trades 38 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Lloyd's of London 6th auction trades 38 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lloyd's of London on Friday issued the results of its sixth auction of capacity for the insurance market's 1997 year.</p>
<p>In this auction, held between 16-19 September, a total of 38 million stg of market capacity was auctioned, realising a total value of 1.15 million stg, Lloyd's said in a statement.</p>
<p>Subscription orders (offers to buy) entered during the sixth auction totalled 246 million stg, while tenders (offers to sell) totalled 61 million stg.</p>
<p>Cumulatively, the six auctions held this year have resulted in 1.27 billion stg of capacity (representing 12 percent of 1996 underwriting capacity) being auctioned, realising 27.2 million stg in respect of 124 Lloyd's syndicates.</p>
<p>The auction was the sixth in the 1996 series of auctions being held from July to October. The seventh auction will be held between 30 September and 3 October. Below are details of this week's syndicate.</p>
